.Dd November 7, 2026
.Dt JABBER_AUTOBUDDY 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm jabber_autobuddy
.Nd manage buddies for the ChatServer XMPP service
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl V
.Op Fl f Ar database
.Ar command ...
.Nm
.Fl h | v
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
adds and removes buddies (roster entries, with presence subscription in
both directions) by editing the SQLite database of ChatServer, the jabberd2
XMPP server.
A
.Ar JID
is
.Ar user Ns @ Ns Ar domain ;
buddies are only made between users of the same domain.
Changes are logged to
.Xr syslog 3 .
.Pp
The commands are:
.Bl -tag -width "-M, --move-domain from to"
.It Fl i , -inituser Ar JID
Add
.Ar JID
to the database, as signing in for the first time would.
The other commands only act on users who are in the database.
.It Fl d , -deleteuser Ar JID
Delete everything the database holds for
.Ar JID ,
and take it off other users' buddy lists.
The system account is not touched.
.It Fl a , -addbuddy Ar JID
Make
.Ar JID
a buddy of every other user.
.It Fl r , -removebuddy Ar JID
Take
.Ar JID
off every other user's buddy list, and them off its list.
.It Fl m , -all
Make every user a buddy of every other user.
.It Fl g , -group Ar group
Make the members of the system group
.Ar group
buddies of each other, listed under a roster group of that name.
The group is also recorded for the server's autobuddy module, which adds
members to each other's buddy lists when they sign in.
Members are the users listed in the group and the users whose primary
group it is.
.It Fl G , -group-by-id Ar gid
The same, naming the group by its numeric ID.
.It Fl u , -ungroup Ar group
Undo
.Fl -group :
remove the buddy pairings between the members of
.Ar group
and stop adding them at sign-in.
.It Fl U , -ungroup-by-id Ar gid
The same, by numeric ID.
.It Fl M , -move-domain Ar from to
Move every user of domain
.Ar from
to domain
.Ar to .
.El
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width "-M, --move-domain from to"
.It Fl f , -database Ar path
The database; the default is
.Pa /var/db/jabberd/sqlite.db .
.It Fl V , -verbose
Report each change on standard error.
.It Fl v , -version
Print the version and exit.
.It Fl h , -help
Print a summary of the commands and exit.
.El
.Pp
Commands may be given more than once and run in this order:
.Fl -deleteuser ,
.Fl -inituser ,
.Fl -removebuddy ,
.Fl -addbuddy ,
then one of
.Fl -all ,
.Fl -group
or
.Fl -ungroup ,
which cannot be combined; then
.Fl -move-domain .
All changes are made in one transaction.
The spellings of Apple's version, such as
.Fl -i
and
.Fl -m ,
are accepted too.
.Pp
Run as root,
.Nm
switches to the owner of the database before it opens it.
Users who are signed in see changes when they next sign in.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/db/jabberd/sqlite.db -compact
.It Pa /var/db/jabberd/sqlite.db
The ChatServer database.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Make the members of the group
.Dq staff
buddies, now and when new members sign in:
.Pp
.Dl jabber_autobuddy --group staff
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pamauth 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in Mac OS X Server, where groups were Open Directory groups
and group IDs were GUIDs.
This version for FreeBSD uses system groups.
